"ir.kfx: the engine's values, its IR, and its continuation's frames
 (docs/research/engine.md, C58). The engine's data lives at `@h`, its heap,
 never freed for now."

"The engine's effect: its heap, and the world, which an FX-26 program's
 I/O is (C49)."
(define-effect eng (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @h) (write @h) (alloc @h)
                           (io stdin) (io stdout) (io stderr) (io clock) (io fs-read) (io fs-write) (io args) (io exit) (io sys) (io terminal)))

"A run's failure (C110): `error`, a trap (`car` of nil, an index out of
 range), or what the engine cannot do. The engine says one here, not by
 failing itself, so that a run that fails is a value its caller sees: the
 machine's step stops at it (`w-failed`), and the REPL ends the entry,
 where a failure would end the REPL, since FX-26 catches none in a
 program's own computation. Its message, the first said; whether one was."
(define engine-failed (ref bool @h) (new #f))
(define engine-failure (ref string @h) (new ""))
"Its backtrace (TODO §29): a line for each procedure, innermost first;
 none until the machine has stopped at it (vm.kfx's `stopped!`), or if
 nothing is known."
(define engine-trace (ref (listof string @h) @h) (new nil))

(define failed-with! (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @h) (write @h)) (string) unit)
  (lambda (message)
    (if (get engine-failed) #u (begin (set engine-failure message) (set engine-failed #t)))))

"The failure said, taken: its message, and none kept."
(define failure-taken! (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @h) (write @h)) () string)
  (lambda ()
    (let ((m (get engine-failure))) (begin (set engine-failed #f) (set engine-failure "") (set engine-trace nil) m))))

(define-rec
  (traced (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @h)) ((listof string @h) string) string)
    (lambda (ls prefix)
      (if (null? ls) "" (string-append "\n" (string-append prefix (string-append (car ls) (traced (cdr ls) prefix))))))))

"The failure said, taken, with its backtrace: each line after its message,
 on a line of its own, after `prefix`."
(define failure-traced! (subr (maxeff (read @globals) spin (read @h) (write @h)) (string) string)
  (lambda (prefix)
    (let* ((t (get engine-trace)) (m (failure-taken!))) (string-append m (traced t prefix)))))

"A value, of any shape: uniform, so that a member of a union is its
 union's value already (C57). Integers of every width are `int`, wrapped
 by their operations. A pair's head and tail are cells, as FX-26's pairs
 may be written. A procedure is its code and the environment it closes
 over; a primitive, its name in the primitives' table; a continuation,
 its frames, up to the prompt it was captured to, and whether it may be
 resumed once only (KFX's `abort-with-continuation`) and was."
(define-datatype val
  (v-int int)
  (v-real f64)
  (v-char char)
  (v-string string)
  (v-symbol symbol)
  (v-bool bool)
  (v-unit)
  (v-nil)
  (v-pair (ref val @h) (ref val @h))
  (v-ref (ref val @h))
  (v-sum string val)
  (v-product strings (arrayof val @h))
  (v-data string (arrayof val @h))
  (v-array (arrayof val @h))
  (v-bytes (bytevectorof @h))
  (v-flat (arrayof val @h))
  (v-proc i64 ir (listof (arrayof val @h) acyclic))
  (v-prim string i64)
  (v-ctor string i64)
  (v-tag i64)
  (v-cont (listof frame acyclic) (ref bool @h) bool)
  (v-datum sexp))

(define-type vals (listof val acyclic))
(define-type env (listof (arrayof val @h) acyclic))

"The IR: names resolved. A local is a frame's depth and slot; a global,
 an index into the globals; a primitive call names its primitive. `let`
 makes a frame of its values; `letrec` makes the frame first, its values
 seeing it. A `tagcase`'s arm binds its variant's fields, or a sum's one
 value, in a frame of its own. A lambda keeps its name, if it is bound to
 one, and where it is written (`file:line`), for a failure's backtrace
 (TODO §29)."
(define-datatype ir
  (i-lit val)
  (i-local i64 i64)
  (i-global i64 string)
  (i-lambda i64 ir string string)
  (i-call ir (listof ir acyclic))
  (i-if ir ir ir)
  (i-seq (listof ir acyclic))
  (i-let (listof ir acyclic) ir)
  (i-letrec (listof ir acyclic) ir)
  (i-define i64 ir)
  (i-sum string ir)
  (i-product strings (listof ir acyclic))
  (i-extract string ir)
  (i-tagcase ir (listof arm acyclic) ir)
  (i-prompt ir ir ir))

"An arm of a `tagcase`: its tag, how many it binds (a datatype's fields,
 or a sum's product's, taken apart), or -1 if it binds the value whole;
 and its body. The default arm binds the value."
(define-datatype arm (arm string i64 ir))

(define-type irs (listof ir acyclic))

"What is done with values once all are found, left to right."
(define-datatype todo
  (t-call)
  (t-let ir)
  (t-product strings))

"A frame of the continuation: what is left of an expression once its
 part being evaluated has a value."
(define-datatype frame
  (k-if ir ir env)
  (k-seq irs env)
  (k-list vals irs env todo)
  (k-letrec (arrayof val @h) i64 irs ir env)
  (k-define i64)
  (k-sum string)
  (k-extract string)
  (k-tagcase (listof arm acyclic) ir env)
  (k-prompt-tag ir ir env)
  (k-prompt-handler val ir env)
  (k-prompt i64 val)
  (k-abort i64))

(define-type frames (listof frame acyclic))
